From: Andrei <andrei@luta.email>
Subject: [PATCH] Link game executables as large address aware

The retail game and the community builds are 32-bit and run with the
default 2GB user address space. Marking the executable large address
aware lets 64-bit Windows give the process a 4GB address space, which
is the single biggest memory-related stability improvement available
without a full 64-bit port. This is the same change the community has
applied to the retail generals.exe for years with LAA patchers.

Applies to both the MSVC and MinGW link steps.
---
 Generals/Code/Main/CMakeLists.txt   | 8 ++++++++
 GeneralsMD/Code/Main/CMakeLists.txt | 8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Generals/Code/Main/CMakeLists.txt b/Generals/Code/Main/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/Generals/Code/Main/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/Generals/Code/Main/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -16,6 +16,14 @@ target_link_libraries(g_generals PRIVATE
     winmm
 )
 
+# Let 64-bit Windows give this 32-bit process a 4GB address space instead of 2GB.
+if(MSVC)
+    target_link_options(g_generals PRIVATE "/LARGEADDRESSAWARE")
+elseif(MINGW)
+    target_link_options(g_generals PRIVATE "-Wl,--large-address-aware")
+endif()
+
+
 # TODO Originally referred to build host and user, replace with git info perhaps?
 file(WRITE ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/GeneratedVersion.h
 "#pragma once
diff --git a/GeneralsMD/Code/Main/CMakeLists.txt b/GeneralsMD/Code/Main/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/GeneralsMD/Code/Main/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/GeneralsMD/Code/Main/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -16,6 +16,14 @@ target_link_libraries(z_generals PRIVATE
     zi_always
 )
 
+# Let 64-bit Windows give this 32-bit process a 4GB address space instead of 2GB.
+if(MSVC)
+    target_link_options(z_generals PRIVATE "/LARGEADDRESSAWARE")
+elseif(MINGW)
+    target_link_options(z_generals PRIVATE "-Wl,--large-address-aware")
+endif()
+
+
 # TODO Originally referred to build host and user, replace with git info perhaps?
 file(WRITE ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/GeneratedVersion.h
 "#pragma once
